MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=1
DESCRIPTION=Start integrating KeyQuorum's identity model from the storage, profile and history side (hosted track, native C, same rules as KeyQuorum's authority hierarchy; no KeyQuorum code or keys yet). Every account now has a heritage key id shaped like a KeyQuorum label: Root is the master account (key Root), the default Flinstone account is Root.Flinstone, a second default account Alternative is Root.Alternative, and an account created while logged in as Flinstone (sudo does not change the creator) is Root.Flinstone.Bob. New normative shard contracts/identity/contract_p2_heritage.h (FL_CONTRACT_P2_IDENTITY_REV 3 -> 4: key id vocabulary, relation and bridge-state enums, home directory layout) and FL_AUTHZ_OP_IDENTITY_BRIDGE = 10 (appended; denied to guests like the other identity ops). kernel/core/identity/heritage.c validates, derives and compares key ids; user_db gains key_id, created_by and created_at columns (added in place), lab seeds Root/root, Flinstone/flinstone and Alternative/alternative behind FL_USERS_LAB_DEFAULTS, account names are [A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,31}, unique and matched case-insensitively (login root still works and signs in as Root), and stores from before heritage migrate on first load (root -> Root, flinstone -> Flinstone, every other account directly under Root; a name that is not a valid segment keeps login but no key id). Authority flows down only: userdel needs an ancestor and refuses an account that still has accounts below it, passwd covers yourself and accounts below you. Bridges (kernel/core/identity/bridge.c, table bridges in the same store) are the only way across branches: one side requests, the other side or an ancestor of it accepts, either side or an ancestor of either revokes; pending grants nothing and a bridge joins exactly its two accounts. With the VM jail active every account has an owner-only home nested like its key id (<jail>/home/Flinstone/Bob); a path in the home tree belongs to the deepest account whose home holds it and is open only to that owner, its ancestors and accounts bridged to it, judged on the canonical path in fs_jail_check_access and the local file provider, and sudo still lifts the outer jail but never heritage; su - starts in the account's home. New shell commands profile [u] (key id, heritage line, creator, creation time, children, home, bridges) and bridge list|request|accept|revoke; login prints the key id. Audit lines (FL_AUDIT=1) gain actor=<key id> on type=shell and type=authz, and account changes emit type=identity events (useradd, userdel, passwd, bridge-request/accept/revoke) with no password; FL1 history is unchanged. Also fixes a leaked SQLite handle when the account store cannot be opened. Tests: new make test_heritage (key ids, relations, seeds, legacy migration, bridges, jail homes; in CI and run_all_tests.sh), test_invariants and test_p0_p2_wiring updated for canonical names. Docs: docs/IDENTITY_HERITAGE.md, kernel/core/identity/README.txt, contracts/identity/README.txt, ROADMAP P2 note and TODO row. Not covered yet: KeyQuorum keys and signed bridges, bridges in server file sharing, sudo -i still reaching Root, and the freestanding kernel and browser lab identities. The account rules now come from KeyQuorum's Rust crate instead of C: heritage key ids, names, the depth limit, relations and home paths are exported from ffi/identity (libkeyquorum_identity.a with include/keyquorum_identity.h), built from the third_party/keyquorum git submodule by make (cargo required). kernel/core/identity/heritage.c is now a set of thin wrappers, so callers and the test suites are unchanged. The bundled SQLite in the library is the one the shell uses. sudo -i asks for Root's password (as su root does) and records type=identity event=sudo-i.

RELEASE_DATE=2026-10-19
